      "problem": "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Find the orthogonal projection of $a$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{b\\}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The orthogonal projection of $a$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{b\\}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{b\\cdot a}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 3+0\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot (-3)+2\\cdot 3}{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{6+0+6+6}{4+0+4+4}b \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{12}b \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}b \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
